            "review_title": "Review at Pasta Fresca",
            "review_text": "Saigon_Charley\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam30 contributions\n0\nWhat a pleasant surprise!\nMar 2018 • Solo\nIt's a tiny place next to a tiny alley in a very local area in HCMC. I just initially wanted to grab a bite, but boy, I was in for a real surprise! \n\nI started with the prosciutto e melone. The balsamic was tad overpowering at first but it grows on you. Finished the entire plate in seconds! The prosciutto serving was quite generous for the price.\n\nPleasant surprise was pici. Pici is a handrolled pasta I was fortunate enough to try in one of my travels in Tuscany and to my utter delight they have it! I ordered it with Atlantic tuna and olives. Divine. It's really very good! \n\nThen followed the squash ravioli. Had it served with cream sauce. Good but quite heavy, sadly they didn't have the pain butter and sage option that I love but this was still good.\n\nVery happy with the food. Service was spot on. The space was to cramped otherwise this visit would've been excellent! \n\nKeep it up and I hope you'd maintain the quality. :)\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 6, 2018",
